+//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
+// Hybrid highlight splat layer (r_DepthOfFieldMode 0)
+//
+// Runs AFTER the full gather above, and only adds what the gather cannot do: scattered bokeh
+// discs for highlights. A gather averages its taps, so a small very bright sample gets flattened
+// into its neighbourhood instead of throwing a disc; this pass puts that missing energy back.
+//
+// One quad per half-resolution pixel is still expanded on the GPU from SV_VertexID - no vertex
+// stream at all, a plain non-indexed triangle list of width * height * 6 vertices - but the
+// vertex shader now discards all but the highlights through a soft-knee luminance threshold, so
+// the surviving quad count is a tiny fraction of the frame and fillrate is bounded. Each survivor
+// carries only the EXCESS energy above the knee (hue preserved), which is what keeps the splat
+// from double counting what the gather already spread.
+//
+// Splats accumulate additively into a near and a far layer, then a single fullscreen pass adds
+// them onto the gathered HDR target.
+//
+// The internal reflection ghosts (LensGhostSpec.md) share those layers and that overlay. A ghost
+// is an image of the APERTURE, which is precisely what a bokeh sprite is, so it is drawn by the
+// same pixel shader and inherits the iris polygon, the shape mask and its rotation, the
+// anamorphic oval, the cat-eye clip and the axial chromatic rim without a line of its own. Every
+// constant that describes the pupil is therefore resolved ONCE below and handed to both draws -
+// that sharing is the whole reason the two live in one function.
+//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
+void CDepthOfFieldStage::ExecuteSplatLayers(const SDepthOfFieldParams& dofParams, const Vec4& vDofParams0, const Vec4& vDofParams1,
