@@ -0,0 +1,259 @@
+# Field-Dependent Pupil (cat-eye, coma, astigmatism) ??Specification
+
+Status: approved for implementation, 2026-08-26. Owner of semantics: the camera manager
+(this document). Implementation: renderer DOF stage + tonemap + shaders + component.
+
+## 1. What this adds
+
+Today the pupil (`iris ??shape mask`, see SpriteBokehSpec / HybridDof 2.0) is evaluated as if
+every pixel looked at the lens straight down the axis. A real lens does not: rays to the edge of
+the field pass the barrel and the element rims obliquely, so the visible pupil is **clipped by
+the mechanical opening**, more the further from the centre. That single fact produces, at once:
+
+* cat-eye bokeh (discs become lens-shaped, long axis tangential) toward the corners,
+* mechanical vignetting (less light through a clipped pupil),
+* edge bokeh that is dimmer than centre bokeh,
+* and all of it fading away as the iris is stopped down (a small pupil is never clipped).
+
+This round upgrades the pupil model from an on-axis 2D pupil to a **field-dependent pupil**, and
+generalises the per-pixel kernel transform so two further field aberrations ride on the same
+plumbing: **coma** (radial comet tails, ??pupil radius簡, strongest wide open) and
+**astigmatism** (radial vs tangential focus split: the blur ellipse elongates radially on one
+side of focus and tangentially on the other).
+
+Physically correct AND bold: defaults are 0 (no change to existing scenes); at strength 1, wide
+open, the corner pupil is cut to a lens shape passing ~40% of the light. The offset can never
+exceed the barrel radius (`K_reach <= 0.97 R_b`): a lens whose barrel slid past the pupil centre
+would not cover its own sensor, and a stopped-down pinhole must pass light everywhere - so
+stopping down always REMOVES the clipping, never blacks the corners out. The natural zone is
+roughly 0.2??.4, 1 is the exaggeration zone (flaw ??suppression ??residual).
+
+## 2. Model
+
+### 2.1 Coordinates
+
+* **Field vector** `f` of a pixel: `f = ((tc - 0.5) * 2) * (A, 1) / sqrt(A簡 + 1)`, with `A` =
+  render target width / height (`PS_ScreenSize.x / PS_ScreenSize.y`, or the VS equivalent).
+  `|f| = 0` at the frame centre, `1` at the frame corners. `u = f / |f|` is the radial unit
+  vector, `t = perp(u)` the tangential one. All three passes below (gather, splat, tonemap) run
+  on the rendered = sensor frame (the anamorphic desqueeze happens later in PostAA), so no
+  squeeze factor enters the field vector.
+* **Pupil units**: 1 = the pupil's bounding radius ??the unit the gather taps and the splat's
+  quad-local coordinates already use (bare iris: iris radius; with a mask: whichever hole
+  bounds the pupil). Physical radius of that bounding circle relative to the lens wide open:
+
+  `p = clamp(N_open / N_geo, 0.05, 1)`, `N_geo = max(N, N_mask)` (`GetGeometricAperture()`),
+  `N_open` = the new **Maximum Aperture** lens parameter.
+
+  Everything field-related is expressed in wide-open pupil units on the CPU and divided by `p`
+  to reach pupil units, so stopping down shrinks the pupil relative to the fixed barrel and the
+  effects vanish by themselves ??no separate "aperture link".
+
+### 2.2 Cat-eye = barrel clip
+
+The mechanical opening is a circle of radius `R_b = 1.05` (wide-open units; cvar
+`r_DofCatEyeBarrel`, tuning only) whose centre, seen from field position `f`, sits at
+`c = -u * (K_reach * catEye * |f|)` with `K_reach = 1.0` (cvar `r_DofCatEyeReach`, clamped to `<= 0.97 R_b`). In pupil
+units: `c_p = c / p`, `R_p = R_b / p`.
+
+* Pupil value at pupil point `x`: `pupil(x) *= saturate((R_p - |x - c_p|) / softEdge)`,
+  `softEdge = 0.08` (gather) / `0.06` (splat). The band is CENTRED on `R_p` (`+ 0.5` inside the saturate) so that with Cat-eye 0 every tap of the unit pupil sits fully inside the 1.05 barrel and the clip is an exact identity.
+* Transmission (fraction of the on-axis light that still gets through), unit disc ??barrel:
+
+  ```
+  T(d, R) = area(disc(1,0) ??disc(R, d)) / ?
+  d >= 1 + R      -> 0
+  d <= R - 1      -> 1            (barrel encloses the pupil)
+  d <= 1 - R      -> R簡           (barrel inside the pupil; not reachable with R_b >= 1)
+  else A = acos((d簡 + 1 - R簡) / (2d)) + R簡 acos((d簡 + R簡 - 1) / (2dR))
+           - 0.5 sqrt((-d + 1 + R)(d + 1 - R)(d - 1 + R)(d + 1 + R)),  T = A / ?
+  ```
+  with `d = K_reach * catEye * |f| / p`, `R = R_b / p`. This is a shared shader function
+  (`LensFieldPupilTransmission(d, R)` in `PostEffectsLib.cfi`, used by DepthOfField.cfx and
+  HDRPostProcess.cfx ??verify both include it; if not, add the include).
+
+The clip is applied to the pupil **before** the aberrations below (it is the aperture; coma and
+astigmatism are what the glass does to the rays that got through).
+
+### 2.3 Where the light loss is applied ??exactly once
+
+This is the semantic rule of the round and the reason the spec exists:
+
+* The **tonemap vignette** darkens every pixel by `T(|f|)`. That is the one and only place the
+  mechanical light loss is applied, because it belongs to in-focus pixels just as much as to
+  blurred ones (the pupil is clipped whether or not the point is in focus).
+* The **gather** clips its taps (weights ? clip) and keeps its existing renormalisation by
+  accumulated weight. It therefore reshapes the kernel without changing brightness ??correct,
+  since the tonemap already carries the loss.
+* The **splat** divides by the full disc area (`fSplatNorm`), so clipping its pupil would dim
+  it by `T` automatically and the tonemap would dim it again (`T簡`). The splat therefore
+  **multiplies its deposit by `1 / max(T, 0.05)`**, computed in the VS from the sprite's own
+  field position with the same function, so gather, splat and tonemap agree to the number.
+* The existing exposure/T-stop path is untouched: the meter reads the axis.
+* The stock gather term `fOptVignettingAmount = 0.2` / `fOptVignetting` in `DofPS` is a crude
+  radial tap squash ??Crytek's own approximation of this effect. **Remove it** (both loops);
+  leaving it would stack two versions of the same thing.
+
+`Vignette Amount` / `Vignette Aperture Link` stay as they are (their math is not changed) but
+they are now the *residual* falloff (glass, sensor microlenses). Update their tooltips to say
+so and point at Cat-eye for the mechanical part.
+
+### 2.4 Coma
+
+Third-order transverse coma displaces a ray by an amount ??field height ? pupil radius簡, along
+the radial direction. In pupil units with the aperture folded in:
+
+`x' = x + u * (K_coma * coma * p * |f| * |x|簡)`, `K_coma = 0.6`.
+
+The `p` factor is what makes coma disappear on stopping down (?_open = ?_pupil 繚 p, and the
+term is ???_open簡). At coma = 1, wide open, in the corner, a rim tap moves 0.6 radii ??a clear
+comet.
+
+### 2.5 Astigmatism
+
+Sagittal and tangential foci differ, so the blur ellipse is elongated radially on one side of
+focus and tangentially on the other:
+
+`x' = u * dot(x,u) * (1 + s * K_astig * astig * |f|簡) + t * dot(x,t) * (1 - s * K_astig * astig * |f|簡)`,
+`K_astig = 0.5`, `s = +1` for the far layer, `-1` for the near layer.
+
+Area-preserving to first order, so no energy bookkeeping. Not aperture-dependent (it is a
+focus shift, not a pupil-size effect).
+
+### 2.6 Anamorphic interaction
+
+The gather taps arrive with `x /= S` already applied on the CPU; the splat quad is narrowed by
+`1/S`. The barrel clip and the aberrations are defined on the **unsqueezed** pupil, so in the
+gather: `x_p = (x.x * S, x.y)` ??clip / coma / astig in pupil space ??`x' = (x_p'.x / S, x_p'.y)`.
+In the splat PS the quad-local coordinate already *is* pupil space (the quad was narrowed), so
+nothing extra is needed there. `S` reaches the gather through the new constant (see 禮4).
+
+## 3. Parameters
+
+### 3.1 Component (`SCineLensParams`, Lens group ??insert BEFORE `bokehShapeTex`, which must stay last for the memcmp)
+
+| Member | Label | Range | Default | Tooltip gist |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| `maxAperture` ('mxap') | Maximum Aperture | `Range<1, 22, 1, 8>` (Schematyc Range takes int template args, same limit as Mask Aperture) | 1.4 | The lens's wide-open f-number. Sets how big the pupil is relative to the barrel: cat-eye and coma are strongest at this f-number and fade as the iris is stopped down from it. Does not clamp Aperture. |
+| `catEye` ('ctey') | Cat-eye | `Range<0, 1, 0, 1>` | 0 | Mechanical clipping of the pupil by the lens barrel toward the frame edges: corner bokeh becomes lens-shaped (long axis tangential), edges darken and their bokeh dims, all fading as the iris closes. 0.2??.4 natural, 1 caricature. Replaces the guessed mechanical part of Vignette Aperture Link. |
+| `coma` ('coma') | Coma | `Range<0, 1, 0, 1>` | 0 | Off-axis highlights grow radial comet tails, strongest wide open, gone when stopped down. |
+| `astigmatism` ('astg') | Astigmatism | `Range<-1, 1, -1, 1>` | 0 | Radial/tangential focus split: off-axis blur stretches radially on one side of focus and tangentially on the other. Sign swaps which side. |
+
+`ReflectType` entries follow the existing pattern. New `Range<>` members animate in TrackView
+automatically.
+
+### 3.2 Post-effect params (`CDepthOfField`, `PostEffects.h` / `PostProcessDOF.cpp` / `PostEffects.cpp` reset)
+
+`Dof_User_CatEye` (0), `Dof_User_PupilScale` (1), `Dof_User_Coma` (0), `Dof_User_Astigmatism`
+(0) ??all `AddParamFloatNoTransition`. `SDepthOfFieldParams` gains `fCatEye`, `fPupilScale`,
+`fComa`, `fAstigmatism` with those defaults and doc comments.
+
+### 3.3 Component ??renderer
+
+In the same place the other `Dof_User_*` values are pushed (`ApplyDof` region around
+`CinematicCameraComponent.cpp:755`):
+
+```
+const float p = clamp_tpl((float)m_lens.maxAperture / GetGeometricAperture(), 0.05f, 1.0f);
+Dof_User_CatEye       = catEye
+Dof_User_PupilScale   = p
+Dof_User_Coma         = coma
+Dof_User_Astigmatism  = astigmatism
+```
+Saved/restored exactly like `Dof_User_MaskRotation` (baseline capture, `RestoreAllEffects`,
+`ClearSavedBaselines`). Restore values put the renderer back to "no field effects".
+
+### 3.4 CVars (`RendererCVars`)
+
+| CVar | Default | Meaning |
+|---|---|---|
+| `r_DepthOfFieldCatEyeBarrel` | 1.05 | Barrel radius in wide-open pupil units (tuning). |
+| `r_DepthOfFieldCatEyeReach` | 1.0 | Barrel offset at the frame corner, per unit Cat-eye (tuning; clamped below the barrel radius). |
+| `r_DepthOfFieldFieldDebug` | 0 | 1 = tonemap outputs the field transmission `T` as grey instead of the picture. |
+
+## 4. Renderer plumbing
+
+### 4.1 `CDepthOfFieldStage::Execute` (DepthOfField.cpp)
+
+Resolve once per frame, next to the existing domain resolution:
+
+```
+vDofFieldPupil  = ( K_reach * catEye / p,   R_b / p,   K_coma * coma * p,   K_astig * astig )
+vDofFieldPupil2 = ( S (squeeze), debug, 0, 0 )
+```
+Expose the derivation as a static helper (`CDepthOfFieldStage::ResolveFieldPupil(catEye, p,
+coma, astig)` ??Vec4) so the tonemap uses the identical numbers. Bind both constants to
+`m_passGather0`, `m_passGather1` (PS) and to the splat primitive (VS + PS). Log once per change:
+`[DOF] field pupil catEye=%.2f p=%.2f -> offset/field=%.2f barrel=%.2f coma=%.2f astig=%.2f`.
+
+### 4.2 Gather (`DofPS`, DepthOfField.cfx)
+
+Per pixel: `f`, `r = |f|`, `u` (guard r < 1e-4 ??u = (1,0), all terms vanish anyway), `t`.
+Per tap, replacing the `fOptVignetting` lines:
+
+```
+float2 x = float2(offset.x * S, offset.y);               // unsqueezed pupil space
+float2 c = -u * (vDofFieldPupil.x * r);
+float  clipW = saturate((vDofFieldPupil.y - length(x - c)) / 0.08);
+float  rad = dot(x, u), tan = dot(x, t);
+float  a = s * vDofFieldPupil.w * r * r;                 // s = -1 near loop, +1 far loop
+float2 xa = u * rad * (1 + a) + t * tan * (1 - a);       // astigmatism
+xa += u * (vDofFieldPupil.z * r * dot(x, x));            // coma
+float2 cocOffset = <coc> * fCocScale * float2(xa.x / S, xa.y);
+```
+Near loop: `wn *= clipW` (weighted path) and `cn *= clipW` (the `SAMPLE0/1` max path, which
+ignores `wn`). Far loop: `wf *= clipW`. The `caccNear/caccFar` renormalisation stays.
+
+### 4.3 Splat (`DofBokehRefVS` / `DofBokehRefPS`)
+
+VS: field vector from `screenProj.xy`; `T = LensFieldPupilTransmission(vDofFieldPupil.x * r,
+vDofFieldPupil.y)`; growth factor `g = 1 + vDofFieldPupil.z * r + abs(vDofFieldPupil.w) * r * r`
+so the deformed shape still fits the quad; `QuadPos.xy *= g`. New interpolator
+`float4 Field : TEXCOORD2 = (f.x, f.y, 1 / max(T, 0.05), g)`.
+
+PS, before the existing pupil evaluation:
+```
+tcQuad *= IN.Field.w;                                   // quad-local -> pupil units: the quad grew by g, the shape did not
+// inverse aberration (draw the deformed shape by sampling the undeformed pupil at M^-1)
+astig: rad /= (1 + a), tan /= (1 - a)   (a as above, s from QuadPos.z: near if > 0.5)
+coma : x0 = x - u * k * |x|簡;  x1 = x - u * k * |x0|簡   (one Newton refinement, k = z * r)
+```
+Then the barrel clip multiplies `fPupil` (soft edge 0.06), the bare-iris `clip(lerp(1 - fLen,
+...))` uses the corrected `tcQuad`, and the final deposit is multiplied by `IN.Field.z`.
+`fSplatNorm` is unchanged (the shape's pixel area is unchanged; only the quad grew).
+
+### 4.4 Tonemap (`ToneMapping.cpp`, `HDRFinalScenePS`)
+
+Read `Dof_User_CatEye` and `Dof_User_PupilScale` through `PostEffectMgr()->GetByName(...)`
+(NOT `CDepthOfField::GetParams()` ??that call advances the TOD focus smoother per call and
+must stay once per frame). `HDRVignetteParams` becomes `(amount, K_reach * catEye / p, R_b / p,
+debug)`. In the shader, after the existing map term:
+```
+fVignetting *= LensFieldPupilTransmission(HDRVignetteParams.y * r, HDRVignetteParams.z);
+if (HDRVignetteParams.w > 0.5) return T as grey;
+```
+The `if (HDRVignetteParams.x > 0.001)` gate must not swallow the new term: the field term
+applies whenever `y > 0`.
+
+## 5. Acceptance
+
+1. Defaults (catEye = coma = astig = 0): pixel-identical to today except for the removal of the
+   stock `fOptVignetting` squash (edge bokeh becomes round instead of slightly radially
+   squeezed ??expected, and more correct).
+2. Cat-eye 0.5, f/1.4 (= Maximum Aperture), a field of point lights: centre discs round, corner
+   discs lens-shaped with the long axis tangential, edges darker; splat and gather silhouettes
+   agree (no bright/dark mismatch between sprite and halo at the edges). `r_DepthOfFieldFieldDebug 1`
+   shows a smooth radial grey falloff.
+3. Same scene, stop down to f/5.6: cat-eye and edge darkening gone; the polygon is intact.
+4. Coma 1, wide open: corner highlights grow radial tails pointing away from the centre;
+   stopped down they vanish. Astigmatism 簣1: corner blur stretches radially on one side of focus,
+   tangentially on the other; sign flips them.
+5. Shape mask + Mask Rotation + anamorphic 2?: cat-eye clips the mask's silhouette (not a
+   circle drawn over it), the oval stays an oval, no double application of the squeeze.
+6. TrackView lists the four new properties. RenderDoc: gather + splat cost change < 0.05 ms at
+   1080p.
+
+## 6. Docs
+
+`README.md` (Lens group table), `docs/ConsoleReference.md` (three cvars), both English. This
+spec is linked from the README's spec list.
