+# Halation Spec
+
+Status: APPROVED FOR IMPLEMENTATION (2026-08-25). Author: main session.
+Repository: `E:\coding3\ReC_sandbox\CRYENGINE_Source`, branch `dev`.
+
+## What it is
+
+On film, light from a very bright source passes through the emulsion, reflects off the film
+base and re-exposes the emulsion around the source. The red-sensitive layer sits deepest, so
+the halo is red-orange, it is much wider than the bright core itself, its edge is soft, and it
+only appears around sources that genuinely overload the emulsion (not around a bright sky).
+It is a property of the film stock, not of the lens, so it does not follow the f-number.
+
+Implementation: a bloom-domain pass next to the diffraction streaks - threshold the scene at a
+halation threshold, blur wide, tint, add into the bloom target with the same bloom-weight
+compensation the streaks use. New param container, new cvar, new component group.
+
+Build with the bundled CMake (`Tools\CMake\Win32\bin\cmake.exe --build solutions_cmake\win64 --target <T> --config Profile`),
+targets `CryRenderD3D11` then `CinematicCamera` (sequentially). Zero errors; zero warnings from
+OUR files (warnings from third-party `Code/SDKs` libraries such as zlib/png16 are pre-existing
+and acceptable - report them separately). Do NOT deploy DLLs or shaders, do NOT commit.
+All comments and docs in English.
+
+---
+
+## A. Renderer param container (`Common/PostProcess/PostProcess.h`, `PostEffects.h/.cpp`, `PostProcess.cpp`)
+
+- `PostProcess.h` enum `EPostEffectID`: add `HDRHalation,` right after `HDRStreaks,` (same
+  "parameter container only" comment).
+- `PostEffects.h`: mirror `SHDRStreaksParams` / `CHDRStreaks` exactly:
+  ```
+  struct SHDRHalationParams { float fAmount = 0; float fThreshold = 2.0f; float fRadius = 0.5f; Vec4 vTint = Vec4(1.0f, 0.35f, 0.15f, 0.0f); };
+  class CHDRHalation : public CPostEffect  // m_nID = EPostEffectID::HDRHalation, m_nRenderFlags = 0
+     params: "HDR_Halation_Amount" (float NoTransition, 0), "HDR_Halation_Threshold" (2.0),
+             "HDR_Halation_Radius" (0.5), "HDR_Halation_Tint" (AddParamVec4NoTransition, (1.0, 0.35, 0.15, 0))
+     Preprocess() -> false, Execute() empty, Reset() resets all four, GetParams() clamps
+     amount 0..3, threshold >= 0, radius 0..1. GetName() "HDRHalation".
+  ```
+- `PostProcess.cpp` (~line 425): `AddEffect(CHDRHalation);` right after `AddEffect(CHDRStreaks);`.
+
+## B. Cvar (`Common/RendererCVars.h/.cpp`)
+
+`r_HDRHalation` (`CV_r_HDRHalation`, int, default 1, VF_NULL), registered next to `r_HDRStreaks`:
+"Film halation: red-orange halo around sources that overload the emulsion, driven by the
+`HDR_Halation_*` post effect params. 0 = off, 1 = on, 2 = diagnostic force mode (amount 1,
+threshold 0.5, radius 0.7, independent of the game-side params)."
+
+## C. Pass (`GraphicsPipeline/Bloom.h/.cpp`)
+
+`Bloom.h`: `CFullscreenPass m_passHalationThreshold; CGaussianBlurPass m_passHalationBlur; CFullscreenPass m_passHalationComposite;`
+(construct with the graphics pipeline like the others; `CGaussianBlurPass` takes
+`CGraphicsPipeline*` too), plus `void ExecuteHalation();`.
+
+`Bloom.cpp`: call `ExecuteHalation();` in `Execute()` right after `ExecuteStreaks();`.
+
+```
+void CBloomStage::ExecuteHalation()
+{
+    if (!CRenderer::CV_r_HDRHalation) return;
+    CHDRHalation* pTech = static_cast<CHDRHalation*>(PostEffectMgr()->GetEffect(EPostEffectID::HDRHalation));
+    if (!pTech) return;
+    SHDRHalationParams p = pTech->GetParams();
+    if (CRenderer::CV_r_HDRHalation == 2) { p.fAmount = 1; p.fThreshold = 0.5f; p.fRadius = 0.7f; }
+    if (p.fAmount < 0.001f) return;
+    PROFILE_LABEL_SCOPE("HDR_HALATION");
+
+    CTexture* pSource = m_graphicsPipelineResources.m_pTexHDRTargetScaled[1][1];   // scratch, free after the streaks
+    CTexture* pTemp   = m_graphicsPipelineResources.m_pTexHDRTargetScaled[1][0];
+
+    // 1. Threshold: reuse technique "HDRStreakThreshold" (same setup pattern as m_passStreakThreshold),
+    //    input m_pTexHDRTargetScaled[0][0], output pSource, StreakParams1 = (threshold, max(threshold*0.25, 0.01), 0, 0).
+    // 2. Blur: m_passHalationBlur.Execute(pSource, pTemp, 1.0f, fDistribution, false) run TWICE
+    //    (a double pass widens the footprint and rounds the profile), with
+    //    fDistribution = 3.0f + 9.0f * clamp(p.fRadius, 0, 1).
+    //    VERIFY the visible width: the halo must read several times wider than the bloom core
+    //    at radius 0.5 on a 1080p frame; if the Gaussian utility's distribution semantics make
+    //    it too tight, raise the multiplier and state the final numbers in the report.
+    // 3. Composite: reuse technique "HDRStreakStretch" with a ZERO step so every tap lands on the
+    //    same texel and the normalised sum is a plain sample:
+    //    StreakParams0 = (0, 0, 0, p.fAmount / fBloomCompositeWeight)   // same bloom-weight divide as the streaks
+    //    StreakParams1 = (0, 0, 1, 0)                                     // decay 1
+    //    StreakParams2 = (tint.rgb, 0)
+    //    state GS_NODEPTHTEST | GS_NOCOLMASK_A | GS_BLSRC_ONE | GS_BLDST_ONE, target m_pTexHDRFinalBloom, source pSource.
+}
+```
+`fBloomCompositeWeight` is computed exactly as in `ExecuteStreaks` (hoist into a small static
+helper or duplicate the four lines - do not change the streaks function's behaviour).
+
+Ordering matters: halation runs AFTER the streaks so the shared scratch targets are free.
+
+## D. Component (`Code/CryPlugins/CinematicCamera/Module/CinematicCameraComponent.h/.cpp`)
+
+New group `SCineHalationParams` (new GUID, label "Halation", memcmp `operator==`), member
+`m_halation` reflected as `'ghal', "Halation", "Halation"` placed right after the Film Grain
+group line (`'ggrn'`).
+
+| member | tag | label | type / range | default | description |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| `amount` | 'hamt' | Halation | Range<0,3,0,2> | 0.0 | Red-orange halo around sources that overload the emulsion: light passes through the film, reflects off the base and re-exposes the red-sensitive layer around the source. A film-stock property, so it does not follow the f-number. 0 = off. |
+| `threshold` | 'hthr' | Halation Threshold | Range<0,50,0,20> | 2.0 | Scene HDR value a source must exceed to halate. High on purpose: a bright sky must not halate, only sources that overload the emulsion. |
+| `radius` | 'hrad' | Halation Radius | Range<0,1,0,1> | 0.5 | How far the halo spreads from the source. |
+| `tint` | 'htnt' | Halation Tint | ColorF | (1.0, 0.35, 0.15, 1) | Colour of the halo. Red-orange for colour negative stock (the red layer sits deepest); a neutral tint mimics a stock with an anti-halation backing partly working. |
+
+`ApplyHalation()` / `RestoreHalation()` with the usual latch (`m_bHalationSaved`, saved
+amount/threshold/radius floats + `Vec4 m_savedHalationTint`; `GetPostEffectParam` /
+`GetPostEffectParamVec4` to save, `SetPostEffectParam` / `SetPostEffectParamVec4` to push):
+- `ApplyHalation` begins with `if (!CanDriveRenderState()) return;`, pushes the four params
+  straight from the properties (amount 0 simply pushes 0).
+- Called from `FinalizeGameCamera()` next to `ApplyFilmGrain()` (game-mode-only category, same
+  as grain). Add `RestoreHalation()` to `RestoreAllEffects()` and `m_bHalationSaved = false`
+  to `ClearSavedBaselines()`.
+
+## E. Docs (English)
+
+- `README.md`: "Halation" property table under the group overview, and a short "## Halation"
