@@ -0,0 +1,140 @@
+# Lens Flaws Pack ??field curvature, edge softness, lateral chromatic aberration
+
+Status: approved for implementation, 2026-08-26. Owner of semantics: the camera manager (this
+document). Companion to FieldPupilSpec.md: same field vector, same pupil scale `p`, same
+"parameters of passes that already run" rule ??this round adds **no render pass**.
+
+## 1. What this adds
+
+The field-dependent pupil made *out-of-focus* edges behave like a real lens. A cheap lens is
+also bad where it is *in focus*: sharp in the centre, soft toward the edges, with coloured
+fringes on high-contrast edges. Three mechanisms, three parameters:
+
+| Mechanism | Parameter | What it does |
+|---|---|---|
+| **Field curvature** (Petzval) | `Field Curvature` (-1..1) | The focal surface is curved: when the centre is in focus the edges focus at a different distance. Positive = edges focus closer than the centre (the usual inward curvature), so a flat subject's edges fall *behind* the focal surface and go far-blurred; negative = the opposite. Independent of aperture as a focus error, but its visibility scales with the CoC like any focus error, so stopping down hides it ??exactly as on a real lens. |
+| **Edge softness** (residual off-axis aberration blur) | `Edge Softness` (0..1) | Even the "in focus" edge is blurred wide open (spherical/oblique aberrations); vanishes stopped down. Implemented as a far-layer CoC floor `??p簡 |f|簡`. |
+| **Lateral chromatic aberration** | `Chromatic Aberration` (0..1) | Magnification depends on wavelength: red and blue are imaged at slightly different radial scales than green. Zero at the centre, growing with field height; red/cyan fringes on contrast edges. Implemented as wavelength-dependent radial remap in the PostAA composite ??it IS distortion, per channel, so it lives in the same coordinate chain as `r_LensDistortion` and composes with squeeze and distortion for free. |
+
+The stock `r_ChromaticAberration` (a separate sharpening/CA full-screen pass in
+`GraphicsPipeline/PostEffects.cpp`) is left untouched and unused: it would cost a pass, and it
+would not follow the `tcFinal` remap.
+
+Bold: at 1, wide open, the corners of a 1080p frame are visibly soft (edge softness) and fringed
+by ~4?? px (CA). Natural zone ~0.2??.4.
+
+## 2. Model
+
+### 2.1 Shared quantities
+
+* Field vector `f`, `r = |f|` (0 centre, 1 corner) exactly as FieldPupilSpec 禮2.1, from the
+  pass's own texture coordinate and `PS_ScreenSize` aspect.
+* Pupil scale `p = clamp(N_open / N_geo, 0.05, 1)` ??already resolved and sent as
+  `Dof_User_PupilScale`.
+
+### 2.2 Field curvature ??inside `ComputeCircleOfConfusion`
+
+`ComputeCircleOfConfusion(depths, ...)` (DepthOfField.cfx) gets the field radius簡 as an extra
+input from its two callers (`DownscaleDofPS` uses `IN.tc2.xy`, `CompositeDofPS` uses
+`IN.baseTC.xy`; the implementer greps for any further caller). Inside:
+
+```
+depthsF = depths * (1 + K_fc * curvature * r簡)      // K_fc = 0.2
+vCocFar  = saturate(depthsF * vDofParamsFocus0.x + vDofParamsFocus0.y)
+vCocNear = saturate(depthsF * vDofParamsFocus0.z + vDofParamsFocus0.w) + FocusRangeNearMin
+```
+`FocusRangeNearMin` (the minimum-Z near blur) keeps the RAW depths ??it is a camera-body
+near-clip effect, not a lens one. Multiplying depth rather than shifting focus keeps the error
+proportional to distance, which is what a curved focal surface does in object space.
+
+Because the splat reads the gather's CoC texture, and the tile min/max chain is built from the
+same downscale output, every consumer sees the same curved focus without further changes.
+
+### 2.3 Edge softness ??CoC floor, far layer only
+
+After the CoC values are formed (same function):
+
+```
+farCoC = max(farCoC, softnessP2 * r簡)                // softnessP2 = K_es * softness * p簡, K_es = 0.35
+```
+Far layer only: an in-focus edge becomes *far*-blurred (it blends behind the near layer as a
+blurred background would), which is the correct layering ??a near-layer floor would make edge
+objects wash over the centre. The composite's `cLayerFar.a = saturate(farCoC)` then blends the
+floor in without any other change. Below the splat fade-in CoC nothing sprites, which is right:
+this is a gentle aberration blur, not bokeh.
+
+### 2.4 Lateral chromatic aberration ??PostAA composite
+
+In `PostAAComposites_PS`, once `tcFinal` is known (after distortion / squeeze):
+
+```
+ca = vLensDistortionParams.w                          // K_ca * amount, K_ca = 0.008
+if (ca > 0)
+{
+    float2 d = (tcFinal - 0.5) * float2(aspect, 1);   // aspect = vLensDistortionParams.y
+    float2 tcR = 0.5 + d * (1 + ca) / float2(aspect, 1);
+    float2 tcB = 0.5 + d * (1 - ca) / float2(aspect, 1);
+    OUT.Color.r = GetTexture2D(PAAComp_CurTarg, PAAComp_LLSS, tcR).r;
+    OUT.Color.b = GetTexture2D(PAAComp_CurTarg, PAAComp_LLSS, tcB).b;
+}
+```
+* `bRemapped` must also be true when `ca > 0` so the main tap uses the sampled path (green
+  stays at `tcFinal`). The sharpening neighbours and the lens-optics taps stay at `tcFinal` ??+  they follow green; the two extra samples are the whole cost.
+* Red magnified, blue shrunk (typical undercorrected glass: red/orange fringe on the outer
+  side of a bright edge, blue/cyan on the inner). No sign parameter; a lens preset that needs
+  the opposite can wait until someone asks.
+* Verify `vLensDistortionParams.w` is unused today; if it is used, add a new constant.
+
+## 3. Parameters
+
+### 3.1 Component (`SCineLensParams`, Lens group, before `bokehShapeTex`)
+
+| Member | Label | Range | Default | Tooltip gist |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| `fieldCurvature` ('fcrv') | Field Curvature | `Range<-1, 1, -1, 1>` | 0 | Curved focal surface: with the centre in focus the edges focus at a different distance. Positive = edges focus closer (a flat wall goes soft toward the edges, far-blurred), negative = edges focus further. Hidden by stopping down, like any focus error. |
+| `edgeSoftness` ('esft') | Edge Softness | `Range<0, 1, 0, 1>` | 0 | Residual off-axis aberration blur: edges stay soft even when in focus, strongest at Maximum Aperture and gone stopped down. The "sharp centre, mushy corners" of cheap and vintage glass. |
+| `chromaticAberration` ('chra') | Chromatic Aberration | `Range<0, 1, 0, 1>` | 0 | Lateral colour fringing: red and blue are magnified differently from green, so high-contrast edges pick up red/cyan fringes that grow toward the frame edges. Zero in the centre. |
+
+### 3.2 Renderer plumbing
+
+* Post-effect params (`CDepthOfField`): `Dof_User_FieldCurvature` (0), `Dof_User_EdgeSoftness`
+  (0) ??`AddParamFloatNoTransition`, reset in `PostEffects.cpp`, copied in
+  `PostProcessDOF.cpp::GetParams` into new `SDepthOfFieldParams::fFieldCurvature` /
+  `fEdgeSoftness` (doc comments).
+* `CDepthOfFieldStage::Execute`: `vDofFieldPupil2 = (S, debug, K_fc * curvature,
+  K_es * softness * p簡)` ??the two free lanes of the existing constant. Bind
+  `vDofFieldPupil2` to `m_passLayerDownscale` and `m_passComposition` as well (both already
+  have `PS_ScreenSize` / `PS_NearFarClipDist`, i.e. the per-view constant buffer; confirm
+  `m_passComposition` has `SetRequirePerViewConstantBuffer(true)` ??add it if missing). Extend
+  the existing once-per-change field-pupil log line with `fc=%.2f es=%.2f`.
+* The splat pass receives `vDofFieldPupil2` already; it does not read the new lanes.
+* CVar `r_LensChromaticAberration` (float, default 0, `VF_NULL`, registered next to
+  `r_LensDistortion`): lateral CA amount 0..1, consumed by `PostAA.cpp` into
+  `vLensDistortionParams.w = K_ca * clamp(value, 0, 1)`.
+* Component `ApplyLensCharacter` / `RestoreLensCharacter`: save / set / restore
+  `r_LensChromaticAberration` exactly like `r_LensDistortion` (new `m_savedLensChromatic`
+  member, captured under the same `m_bLensCharSaved` latch). Editor-live like the other lens
+  character cvars. Push `Dof_User_FieldCurvature` / `Dof_User_EdgeSoftness` in `ApplyDOF`
+  with save / restore like `Dof_User_CatEye`.
+
+## 4. Acceptance
+
+1. All three at 0: pixel-identical to today (`ComputeCircleOfConfusion` reduces to the old
+   formula, `ca = 0` skips the two samples).
+2. Field Curvature +1, f/1.4, camera square to a textured wall focused at the centre: the
+   wall's edges blur (far layer), the centre stays sharp; f/8 brings them back. -1 inverts the
+   direction of the focus error (the edges go sharp when the centre is focused slightly behind
+   the wall).
+3. Edge Softness 1 wide open: the corners are unmistakably soft with the whole frame in focus;
+   f/5.6 (p ??0.25 ??p簡 ??0.06) makes it nearly vanish.
+4. Chromatic Aberration 1: bright/dark edges near the frame border show red on the outer side,
+   cyan on the inner; the centre is clean. With squeeze 2? and distortion 0.5 the fringes follow
+   the remapped picture (no ghost, no double image). SMAA 2TX / TSAA sharpening on: no ghost.
+5. TrackView lists the three new properties. RenderDoc: PostAA composite +2 samples only, DOF
+   downscale/composite unchanged in pass count.
+
+## 5. Docs
+
+`README.md` (Lens table), `docs/ConsoleReference.md` (`r_LensChromaticAberration`), both
+English. Spec listed in the README's spec section.
