+++ b/Code/CryPlugins/CinematicCamera/LensGhostSpec.md
@@ -0,0 +1,154 @@
+# Lens Ghosts ??Specification
+
+Status: approved for implementation, 2026-08-26. Owner of semantics: the camera manager.
+Re-uses the sprite bokeh splat pass (SpriteBokehSpec / HybridDof 2.0 / FieldPupilSpec /
+AxialChromaticSpec): ghosts are drawn by the SAME pixel shader as the bokeh sprites, so they
+carry the iris polygon, the shape mask and its rotation, the anamorphic oval, the cat-eye clip
+and the axial CA rim for free. Only the vertex shader differs.
+
+## 1. What this adds
+
+A strong light in the frame reflects between the lens surfaces and lands on the sensor as a
+chain of **images of the aperture**, strung along the line from the light through the frame
+centre and out the other side. Every element pair adds one ghost with its own size and its
+coating's colour. Modern multi-coated glass shows them faintly; vintage and anamorphic glass
+shows them boldly.
+
+Screen-space HDR extraction, not light-entity flares: anything bright enough ??a lamp, an
+emissive surface, a reflection ??spawns ghosts, and they read the true pupil shape.
+
+## 2. Model
+
+For a bright source at NDC position `P` (frame centre = 0), ghost `i` of `N` sits at
+
+`G_i = -P * k_i`,   `k_i = spread * lerp(0.3, 1.6, i / max(N - 1, 1))`
+
+(so the chain runs from near the centre to past the opposite edge), with radius
+
+`r_i = size * lerp(0.6, 1.4, i / max(N - 1, 1)) * H * 0.05 * p`
+
+in pixels (`H` = frame height, `p` = pupil scale `N_open / N_geo` ??a ghost is an image of the
+aperture, so it shrinks when the iris closes), colour
+
+`c_i = excess * amount * tint rotated in hue by i * hueSpread * 120簞`
+
+(`excess` = the source's luminance above the ghost threshold with the same quadratic knee the
+splat uses, times `p簡` - the energy a ghost carries goes with the aperture AREA like everything
+else the lens passes, and since the disc area is also ??p簡 the per-pixel brightness relative to
+the scene is constant at every f-number: stopping down makes ghosts smaller and harder-edged,
+never brighter (the first cut lacked this and produced blazing specks at f/8 that then grew
+streaks); the bokeh splat's user Highlight Gain is divided out so presets do not couple; the hue rotation is the cheap stand-in for different coatings on different
+surfaces ??one base tint, the rest fan out around it), deposited energy-conservingly over the
+disc exactly as a bokeh sprite is (`fSplatNorm` with `QuadPos.w = r_i`, `Field.z`, dither).
+
+Ghosts are formed in the lens, not in the scene: they are NOT depth-masked and NOT blurred by
+the depth of field. They are drawn as **near** layer quads (`QuadPos.z = 1`), so they are added
+unmasked; the far layer is depth-masked against in-focus foreground and would cut them. They go
+into a layer of their own, composited later ??see 3.4.
+
+## 3. Renderer
+
+### 3.1 Pass structure (`DepthOfField.cpp`)
+
+`ExecuteSpriteBokeh` becomes `ExecuteSplatLayers(bool bSplat, bool bGhost)`: acquire + clear
+the layers, draw the bokeh splat if `bSplat` (`CV_r_DofMode == 0`, as today), draw the ghost
+layers if `bGhost` (`fGhostAmount > 0.001`) into their own target (3.4), then the existing
+overlay composite if `bSplat`. `Execute()` calls it when either is true. All the per-frame constants the splat resolves (`vAspectRatio`,
+`vDofBokehShape`, `vDofBokehMask/2`, `vDofFieldPupil/2`, `vDofAxialChromatic`, the pupil-fill
+gain division) are resolved once and shared by both draws ??that is the point of the re-use.
+
+Ghost draws: technique `DofBokehGhost` = new VS `DofBokehGhostVS` + the existing
+`DofBokehRefPS`, one `CRenderPrimitive` draw per ghost layer (`N <= 6`), each with its own
+`vDofGhost0 = (k_i, r_i, threshold, knee)` and `vDofGhost1 = (tint_i.rgb, amount)`. The grid
+is **quarter resolution** (one quad per 4x4 native pixels; its own per-view CB / viewport like
+the splat's half-res grid): ghost sources are large and the layers multiply the vertex work.
+Same render state (additive), same textures (scene target t0, depth t1 unused, dither t2,
+shape t3), same PS constants.
+
+Once-per-change log: `[DOF] ghosts n=%d amount=%.2f spread=%.2f size=%.2f thresh=%.1f`.
+
+### 3.2 `DofBokehGhostVS` (DepthOfField.cfx)
+
+Mirror of `DofBokehRefVS` with these differences:
+
+* Cell ??`screenProj` as today (the grid is quarter res through the per-view CB, so the
+  existing integer walk works unchanged); the four selection taps sit at 簣0.5 native texel
+  around the cell centre (the middle 2x2 of the 4x4 cell).
+* Threshold / knee from `vDofGhost0.zw` (not `vDofBokehHighlight`); cull on zero excess.
+* No CoC read, no fade, no depth: `fRadiusPx = vDofGhost0.y`; cull if `< 1`.
+* Position: `OUT.Position.xy = -vOutPos.xy * vDofGhost0.x` (NDC mirror through the centre),
+  then the quad expansion exactly as the splat (`QuadPos.xy` from the radius in pixels ?
+  `g_VS_ScreenSize.zw * 2`, `vAspectRatio.xy`, the squeeze `vAspectRatio.z`, the field growth
+  `g`, `Field = (f, 1/T, g)` computed from the GHOST's position, not the source's).
+* `QuadPos.z = 1` (near layer), `QuadPos.w = fRadiusPx`, `Color.w = sqrt(fRadiusPx)`.
+* `Color.rgb = cExcess * 0.25 * vDofGhost1.rgb * vDofGhost1.w`.
+
+### 3.3 Parameters
+
+New component group `SCineGhostParams` "Lens Ghosts" (own GUID, 4CC ids not colliding):
+
+| Member | Label | Range | Default | Tooltip gist |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| `amount` ('ghAm') | Amount | `Range<0, 2, 0, 1>` | 0 | Strength of the internal-reflection ghosts. 0 = off (no pass runs). Modern multi-coated glass ~0.2, vintage ~0.6, above 1 for show. |
+| `count` ('ghCn') | Count | `Range<1, 6, 1, 6, int>` | 3 | Number of ghosts per source ??roughly the number of reflecting element pairs. |
+| `spread` ('ghSp') | Spread | `Range<0.2, 2, 0.5, 1.5>` | 1 | How far the chain reaches from the centre toward the opposite side of the frame. |
+| `size` ('ghSz') | Size | `Range<0.2, 3, 0.5, 2>` | 1 | Ghost diameter, 1 ??5% of frame height wide open. Shrinks with the iris like the aperture it images. |
+| `threshold` ('ghTh') | Threshold | `Range<1, 64, 2, 16>` | 8 | Scene HDR luminance a source needs to spawn ghosts. Far above the bokeh threshold: only lamps, the sun, hot reflections. |
+| `tint` ('ghTn') | Tint | ColorF | (0.6, 0.8, 1.0) | Coating colour of the first ghost; the others fan out around it by Hue Spread. |
+| `hueSpread` ('ghHu') | Hue Spread | `Range<0, 1, 0, 1>` | 0.3 | How far successive ghosts' colours rotate away from Tint (1 = a third of the colour wheel per ghost). |
+
+Post-effect params: `Dof_User_GhostAmount` (0), `Dof_User_GhostCount` (3),
+`Dof_User_GhostSpread` (1), `Dof_User_GhostSize` (1), `Dof_User_GhostThreshold` (8),
+`Dof_User_GhostHueSpread` (0.3), `Dof_User_GhostTint` (`AddParamVec4NoTransition`,
+(0.6, 0.8, 1, 0)); `SDepthOfFieldParams` gains the matching fields. Component `ApplyDOF`
+pushes them (tint via `SetPostEffectParamVec4`, see the halation tint), with save / restore
+like the rest. Hue rotation of the per-layer tints is done on the CPU in the stage
+(RGB ??hue rotate by `i * hueSpread * 120簞`, keep luminance).
+
+Amount is game-mode + editor-live like the other DOF params (it rides `ApplyDOF`).
+
+### 3.4 Pipeline placement
+
+Ghosts do NOT go into the splat layers (the first cut did, and it was wrong). The splat overlay
+runs inside the DOF stage and adds into `$HDRTarget`, which the glare family thresholds
+afterwards for its light sources ??so every ghost above the glare threshold grew its own
+diffraction streaks, anamorphic flare and filter star. Physically a ghost is already a
+second-order internal reflection; a flare struck off one is third order, ~1/50??/200 of the
+ghost, and invisible. **Ghosts are not light sources.**
+
+So the ghost draws accumulate into a dedicated full-resolution RGBA16F layer
+(`$DofGhostLayer`, allocated only on frames ghosts run, cleared each such frame, dropped on
+resize), and `CDepthOfFieldStage::ExecuteGhostComposite()` ??a single full-screen
+`GS_BLSRC_ONE | GS_BLDST_ONE` pass, technique `DofGhostComposite` ??adds it into
+`$HDRTarget` from `CStandardGraphicsPipeline::ExecuteHDRPostProcessing`, immediately after
+`CBloomStage::Execute()`. That point is after the half- and quarter-resolution downsamples of
+the HDR target, i.e. after every thresholded source has been extracted (bloom, streaks,
+anamorphic flare, front filter PSF, halation) and after auto exposure has metered, and before
+the tone map, which is the last reader of the target. The call is unconditional, so **bloom off
+changes nothing**: the ghosts appear at the same place in the frame either way. Being past
+motion blur is also correct ??a ghost is formed in the glass and follows its source, not the
+geometry behind it ??and it stays undepth-masked as before.
+
+Consequences, accepted: ghosts are not halated (halation's source is thresholded earlier), do
+not bloom, and do not drive auto exposure. With the sprite splat off (`r_DepthOfFieldMode 1`)
+the splat overlay pass is now skipped entirely ??the ghosts no longer need it. Cost: one
+full-screen additive pass on frames with ghosts, nothing at all when `Amount <= 0.001`.
+
+## 4. Acceptance
+
+1. Amount 0: no ghost draw, no cost, frame identical.
+2. Amount 0.6, count 3, a lamp in the upper left: three discs along the line through the
+   centre toward the lower right, growing along the chain, coloured around the tint; moving
+   the camera so the lamp crosses the centre makes them cross back through it.
+3. f/1.4 ??f/8: ghosts shrink (aperture image); 6-blade iris ??hexagonal ghosts; a shape mask
+   ??mask-shaped ghosts; Mask Rotation turns them.
+4. Anamorphic 2?: oval ghosts. Cat-eye 0.5: ghosts near the edges are clipped like the bokeh.
+5. Ghosts are not blurred by the DOF and are not cut by an in-focus foreground object standing
+   in front of their position (near-layer overlay). Sprite bokeh OFF (`r_DepthOfFieldMode 1`)
+   with ghosts on: ghosts still draw.
+6. RenderDoc: 3 layers at 1080p < 0.1 ms in a scene with a few sources.
+
+## 5. Docs
+
+README: new "Lens Ghosts" group table + a paragraph in the lens-character chapter; spec listed.
+ConsoleReference unchanged (no cvar).
