+
+## Lens character: vignette and distortion
+
+These are applied through cvars (`r_HDRVignetteAmount`, `r_LensDistortion`,
+`r_LensChromaticAberration`), overwritten every frame while the camera drives the render state
+(in the editor too) and restored when it stops; the console can still audition values when no
+cinematic camera is active. Chromatic Aberration is passed through as authored, 0-1; the
+renderer turns it into the radial scale split.
+
+```
+wideOpenness = clamp((5.6 - N) / (5.6 - 1.4), 0, 1)
+vignette     = VignetteAmount * (1 + VignetteApertureLink * (wideOpenness - 1) * 0.85)
+
+focalTerm  = log2(35 / f_eff)
+distortion = clamp(Distortion + DistortionFocalLink * focalTerm * 0.5, -1, 1) * 0.35
+```
+
+### Lens ghosts
+
+A strong light in the frame does not only pass through the glass; it also reflects back and
+forth between the element surfaces, and each element pair sends one more copy of the **aperture
+itself** onto the sensor. Those copies land on the line from the source through the frame centre
+and out the other side, growing along the chain, each tinted by the coating that reflected it.
+Modern multi-coated glass shows them faintly, vintage and anamorphic glass shows them boldly,
+and moving the camera so the source crosses the centre makes the whole chain cross back
+through it.
+
+This is screen-space, not light-entity flares: anything bright enough - a practical lamp, an
+emissive surface, a hot reflection - throws a chain, and it reads the true pupil shape. That
+comes for free, because a ghost is an image of the aperture and so is a bokeh sprite: the
+renderer draws the ghosts with the **same pixel shader as the sprite bokeh splat**, only a
+different vertex shader, so they carry the iris polygon, the shape mask and its rotation, the
+anamorphic oval, the cat-eye clip and the axial chromatic rim without a line of their own, and
+they shrink with the iris the way the pupil does. Being formed inside the lens, they are neither
+blurred by the depth of field nor cut by an in-focus foreground, and they still draw with the
+sprite bokeh turned off (`r_DepthOfFieldMode 1`). A ghost is also not a light source: it is
+composited into the frame after the glare family has taken its sources, so a ghost never grows
+diffraction streaks, an anamorphic flare or a filter star of its own - a flare off a
+second-order reflection would be a third-order one, and there is nothing there to see. Full
+model in [LensGhostSpec.md](LensGhostSpec.md).
+
